xposes and how it is built.",{"_94":386},"platform/pqc/go-toolchain.mdx",{"_69":388,"_76":115,"_90":-7,"_71":389},"en:_8","Platform support",{"_69":391,"_76":87,"_71":46,"_81":392,"_90":-7,"_10":45,"_92":393},"en:platform/pqc/keys-and-cas.mdx","Create post-quantum keys and CAs, sign with them and issue certificates, with the engine support, API values and constraints that apply.",{"_94":394},"platform/pqc/keys-and-cas.mdx",{"_69":396,"_76":87,"_71":55,"_81":397,"_90":-7,"_10":54,"_92":398},"en:platform/pqc/related-certificates.mdx","Bind a certificate with a post-quantum key to an existing classical certificate of the same device, following RFC 9763, and how Lamassu issues and checks them.",{"_94":399},"platform/pqc/related-certificates.mdx",{"_69":401,"_76":87,"_71":28,"_81":402,"_90":-7,"_10":27,"_92":403},"en:platform/pqc/dashboard.mdx","How the web interface exposes post-quantum algorithms when creating keys, CAs and certificates, and how it displays them.",{"_94":404},"platform/pqc/dashboard.mdx",{"_69":406,"_76":115,"_90":-7,"_71":407},"en:_9","Deployment",{"_69":409,"_76":87,"_71":58,"_81":410,"_90":-7,"_10":57,"_92":411},"en:platform/pqc/tls-front-proxy.mdx","The Traefik fork that terminates device TLS with classical and post-quantum certificates for the same host, how it picks a certificate and how it is built.",{"_94":412},"platform/pqc/tls-front-proxy.mdx",{"_69":414,"_76":87,"_71":31,"_81":415,"_90":-7,"_10":30,"_92":416},"en:platform/pqc/deployment.mdx","Deploy Lamassu with a Traefik front proxy that serves classical, post-quantum and composite certificates, using the chart values or the fast-lane installer.",{"_94":417},"platform/pqc/deployment.mdx",{"_69":419,"_76":115,"_90":-7,"_71":420},"en:_10","Integration tests",{"_69":422,"_76":87,"_71":43,"_81":423,"_90":-7,"_10":42,"_92":424},"en:platform/pqc/integration-tests/overview.mdx","Evidence that software outside Lamassu negotiates post-quantum key exchange and verifies post-quantum and composite cert